{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"5e671a9f97c676eb","name":"card_event_surging_power","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Homefront/events/card_event_surging_power","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SURGING POWER","text":"Give the top four units of your deck +1+1, +2+2, +3+3 and +4+4 respectively.","flavorText":"In January 1942, just weeks after the attack on Pearl Harbor, the US government established the War Production Board to direct the nation’s industrial mobilization. With factories still adjusting to the demands of global war, the Board’s mission was to prioritize military needs, allocate raw materials, and standardize production. It moved quickly, suspending civilian automobile manufacturing and redirecting steel, rubber, and aluminum toward tanks, ships, and aircraft. Although its early months were plagued by overlapping jurisdictions and logistical bottlenecks, the Board soon became the engine of American industrial power. It organized the mass production of everything from rifles to bombers, bringing thousands of civilian firms under military contracts. Giants like Ford, General Motors, and Chrysler successfully retooled their assembly lines for war. By the end of 1942, the results were undeniable. American factories were rolling out over 4,000 aircraft and nearly 1,500 tanks every month. This foundation, laid during the uncertain first year of the conflict, enabled a sustained industrial campaign that would eventually overwhelm the Axis powers with sheer material strength.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_surging_power","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_surging_power_title","SourceString":"SURGING POWER","LocalizedString":"SURGING POWER"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_surging_power_text","SourceString":"